module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.census_row_shape_moved_without_moving_its_consumer

import std.types { String, NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

// REGISTERED BY PR #14574'S REVIEW (review 83899): the PR narrowed a real-route control to the b-side
// because the a-side member no longer exists on the route, and recorded that fact in `//`. A status in
// a comment is a status nobody can read (DESIGN 4c: a status belongs in a typed carrier), and a class
// below the ceiling must name its next-rung trigger (DESIGN 4b meta-obligation 2). This row is the
// carrier for that dropped rung, with the trigger.

data census_row_shape_moved_without_moving_its_consumer: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "census_row_shape_moved_without_moving_its_consumer" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "a census row's shape or stage moved and its consumer was left reading the old fact: the native census classifies each refused module into a cause-group member keyed by (path, reason, stage), attributed to a root by import-reachability. A move to where a refusal is FILED -- which stage owns it, which module heads the chain, whether a module is a root at all -- silently changes what every downstream claim sees, because the claims assert on the SHAPE (which members exist, which stage, what fan-out), not on a contract. Nothing refuses a shape move: no migration, no consumer census, no typed notice. The consumer keeps asserting against a fact that is no longer produced, and reads red.",

    "THE TELL: a cascade or fan-out claim fails with a member MISSING or a STAGE changed, while the fixture text is byte-identical to the run where it passed. The claim is not wrong about the behavior it was written against; the behavior moved out from under it. The reader who takes the claim at face value 'fixes' a compiler that is behaving correctly under its current law, or 'corrects' an expectation that was never wrong.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: a claim that never executed green is not this class (that is registered fill debt, and the ledger says so -- see the specimen's own status); a fixture whose TEXT drifted is not this class (that is drift in the subject, and the diff shows it); a shape move WITH a consumer sweep that updates every consumer in the same change is not this class either -- that is the repair this row's trigger asks for.",

    "SPECIMEN, measured 2026-10-21, runner cells (binary built at each cell's tree, claims run from the same tree). The three claims test.claim.native_census.infer_cascade / census_infer_provider_cascade_is_one_root_with_fan_out_one_holds, test.claim.native_census.cascade_root_fan_out / census_linear_cascade_is_one_wall_with_fan_out_two_holds and ... / census_diamond_cascade_counts_modules_not_paths_holds fail on every tree that loads, from #13929 (51b71cbaec9f, 2026-10-16 06:09) through main. Their fixture sources are byte-identical across the whole window; the probe readouts localize the movement: the b-side module's refusal moved from RESOLVE (the claim's expectation: a resolve root with a fan-out member) to the FRONT END as FileRefusalAtUnresolvedNode (observed own fan-out 2), and a's infer-stage member left the infer fold (its refusal is now filed at resolve), so the a-side member the route claims assert on does not exist. Two of the three (provider_cascade, diamond) are registered ActiveFillDebt in v2.workflow.floor_pure_producer_share's ledger; the linear one is NOT registered, and none of the three has ever been executed green post-#13850 (the cells at #13850's own commit, 983dcb58d5cc, RC=101 on a loader panic at cli_run/entry_resolve.rs:1679 -- a different defect, fixed by #13929; the cells from #13929 on, RC=1).",

    "THE NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the three named claims go green -- executed on the runner with their a-side members present, which requires the census stage/fold authority (v2.compiler.source_root_eval's classification of unresolvable-import refusals: resolve root vs front-end FileRefusalAtUnresolvedNode, and the one-hop import-target attribution) to be adjudicated against the claims' intent: either the producer returns to the shape the claims assert (the b-side refusal filed at resolve with a fan-out member; the a-side member kept in the infer fold), or the expectations are corrected WITH A REASON and the move is then no longer this class. Dissolution condition: every one of the three claims green, or replaced by claims that name the current shape and say why it is right. Until then they are registered fill debt (two of three in v2.workflow.floor_pure_producer_share's ledger; the linear claim's registration is part of the same repair).",

    "THE COST OF THE MISSING NOTICE, one sentence: three sessions spent runner-hours bisecting a 'regression' that was a shape move with no consumer, while the claim text -- the only surviving statement of the intended shape -- sat unchanged and red, indistinguishable from a real defect report.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
